Article 4

Every Woman has the right:
a. to life and the right to maintain life and livelihood;
b. to form a family and continue offspring through lawful marriage;
c. to develop themselves through the fulfillment of their basic needs;
d. to obtain education and benefit from science and technology, arts and culture, in order to improve the quality of life and for the welfare of humanity;
e. to advance themselves in fighting for their rights collectively to build society, nation and state;
f. to recognition, guarantee, protection and fair legal certainty as well as equal treatment before the law;
g. to work and receive fair and proper remuneration and treatment in employment relations;
h. to obtain equal opportunities in government;
i. to freedom of association, assembly and expression of opinion;
j. to protection of self, family, honor, dignity and property under their control, and the right to a sense of security and protection from threats of fear to do or not do something that is a human right;
k. to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and the right to obtain political asylum from other countries;
l. to live prosperously physically and spiritually, to reside and obtain a good and healthy living environment, and the right to obtain health services;
m. to social security that enables their full development as dignified human beings;
n. to equality of position in law and government;
o. to work and a livelihood worthy of humanity; p. in the defense of the state;
q. to communicate and obtain information to develop their personal and social environment, and the right to seek, obtain, possess, store, process, and convey information using all types of available channels;
r. to embrace their respective religions and to worship according to their religion and beliefs; and
s. to obtain education.

